# PatternFly UX Design System — Opinionated Implementation

When building frontend UI in this project, follow these opinionated PatternFly patterns. This ensures consistency across feature teams and reduces cognitive load for users.

## Philosophy

Our UX is designed around the **supervisor** mental model — an operator who must understand, trust, and intervene in complex automation across scale.

- **Standardized compositions** — Combine atomic PatternFly components into larger, prescribed compositions (e.g., a "complete table view" with specific pagination, filtering, and bulk action patterns). These compositions are the unit of consistency.
- **Data-driven adjustments** — Use side-out panels instead of modals for node configuration to preserve workflow canvas context.
- **No custom one-offs** — When PatternFly does not meet a requirement, collaborate via the PatternFly liaison path. Never build a custom component.

## AO Design System

How the AO UI is anchored:

- **Foundation** — Built on top of [PatternFly](https://www.patternfly.org/) for components, patterns, and accessibility baselines
- **Layout** — Page and shell structure follow PatternFly's **Compass** layout architecture
- **Theming** — Visual treatment uses PatternFly's **Unified Theme**
- **Icons** — Based on the [Red Hat design system](https://ux.redhat.com/) [icon set](https://ux.redhat.com/foundations/iconography/#ui-icons), NOT standard PatternFly defaults
- **Automation builder** — Based on [React Flow](https://reactflow.dev/) with PatternFly as visual wrapper
- **Accessibility** — Must achieve [WCAG 2.1 AA](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG2AA-Conformance) and [Section 508](https://www.section508.gov/) compliance
- **PatternFly gaps** — Check PF docs first → Raise with UX (@ansible-ux) → Engage PatternFly → Document with `patternfly-override` Jira label → Resolve upstream

## Page Layout (MANDATORY)

Every page must follow this structural hierarchy:

| Layer | Component | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| App Shell | `Compass` | Overall application frame |
| Navigation | `AppDockedNav` | Left sidebar with icons |
| Page Content | `CompassContent` + `NxPage` | Main content area wrapper |
| Page Header | `NxPageHeader` | Page title and actions |
| Content Frame | `NxPanel` | `Panel` → `PanelMain` → `PanelMainBody` |
| Main Content | Table / Canvas / Form | Primary page content |
| Footer (tables) | Pagination component | Navigation between table pages |

### Page Header Types
- **Main page header** — Left-aligned title, right-aligned actions
- **Details page header** — Left-aligned back button + title, right-aligned actions
- **Form page header** — Left-aligned title, right-aligned actions

### Structure Checklist
- Use `NxPage` as outer wrapper
- Use `NxPageHeader` for title and actions
- Use `StackItem isFilled` + `NxPanel isFullHeight` for content
- Primary action is the rightmost button
- Canvas views use `hasNoPadding`

## Navigation

Use a docked icon navigation (left sidebar) with PatternFly's flyout panels component.

- Hover on nav item (no children) → tooltip with label
- Hover on nav item (has children) → flyout panel with sub-items
- Click nav item (no children) → navigate to route
- Click nav item (has children) → navigate to first enabled child route
- Mouse leaves flyout → close after 150ms grace period

## Filter Bar

- Use PatternFly's Attribute Search component
- Default filter type: "Keyword" search (`contains` filter on all content)
- Filter bar is visible when data exists or when filters are active
- Filter bar is hidden only when the resource type has never had data created
- Filter select dropdowns hide `SearchInput` when fewer than 10 static options; async filters always show search

## Table Component

- ALWAYS use `ScrollableTableContainer` wrapper — this applies the standard table variant by default
- `ScrollableTableContainer` does not set `variant="compact"` — the default (standard) variant is used for main data tables
- Use `variant="compact"` only for dense, supplementary tables (e.g., activity state tables inside panels) where space is constrained
- ALWAYS include `<Thead>` with column headers
- Actions column is rightmost (no column header label)
- All row actions live inside a kebab menu (⋮) — no direct buttons in the actions column
- Action order in kebab: non-destructive first, divider, destructive last
- On the details page header, same actions appear in a kebab; frequently used actions promoted to direct buttons
- Columns should be sortable if applicable
- Clicking resource name navigates to details view
- "Created"/"Modified" columns: username (linked) + date together
- Text-heavy columns (names, descriptions, emails, URLs) MUST use `<Truncate>` — ellipsis with tooltip on hover; `table-layout: fixed` for equal column distribution (do not opt out with `useFixedLayout={false}`)
- Expandable rows: pass `isExpandable` to `ScrollableTableContainer`, add expand-all/collapse-all toggle in `<Thead>` via `expand` prop, use `ExpandableRowContent` for nested detail, compact gray `Label` for list data
- Footer/pagination: cursor-based via `ScrollableTableContainer`'s `footer` prop (`TableFooterProps`)
  - Left: item count — `"5 workflows (of 100 total)"`
  - Right: Previous / Next buttons using API cursor tokens (`prev`, `next`) — no page numbers or per-page selector
  - Pass `{ content, prev, next, onPrev, onNext }` to the `footer` prop

## Form Component

- Use PatternFly's Basic Form component
- Left-aligned, one column, max-width of 600px
- Header: title + primary action button + secondary cancel
- Use typeahead for lists with 10+ options
- Use Read-only Clipboard Copy for system-pre-populated values
- Use Validated component for form validation
- Use Number Input for number fields
- Use popover help text on form field labels
- Use `HelperText` / `HelperTextItem` below inputs for brief contextual guidance (formats, ranges, constraints); popover is for longer descriptions; validation errors replace helper text when invalid
- Use Zod + react-hook-form for validation (project standard)

## Details Component

- Use `DescriptionList isCompact isHorizontal`
- Group related fields using headers
- Consistent date/duration formatting per PatternFly Date/Time guidelines
- Header: title + primary actions from the table row

## Empty States

Use PatternFly's Basic Empty State component. Empty states replace the main content area.

| Scenario | Title | CTA | Filter? |
|---|---|---|---|
| No data | `"No [resources] yet"` | `"Create [resource]"` if applicable | No |
| No filter results | `"No results found"` | `"Clear all filters"` | Yes, with active filters |
| Service error | `"Unable to load [resources]"` | `"Retry"` | No |

Icons per scenario: No data → `PlusCircleIcon` (gray, `lg`), No results → `SearchIcon` (gray, `sm`), Error → `ExclamationCircleIcon` (`status="danger"`, `lg`), No access → `LockIcon` (gray, `lg`), Config required → `WrenchIcon` (gray, `lg`), Success → `CheckCircleIcon` (`status="success"`, default/`xl`), Getting started → `RocketIcon` (gray, `xl`). Use `status` prop for color on status empty states; non-status icons are gray by default. Variant sizing: `sm` in tables/modals, `lg` full-page, `xl` onboarding/success.

## CRUD Patterns

Action verb pairings: "Create" ↔ "Delete", "Add" ↔ "Remove" (AO-internal resources), "Add" ↔ "Disconnect" (external resources), "Assign" ↔ "Unassign"

### Create
- **Full page:** 5+ fields, multi-step wizards
- **Modal:** 2–4 simple fields, quick creation without leaving context

### Read/Detail
- Full page for resources with rich information

### Update/Edit
- **Full page:** 5+ fields, multi-step, or if create is full page
  - Pre-populate fields, track dirty state, warn on unsaved navigation, show loading while saving
- **Modal:** 2–4 fields, or if create is a modal
- **Inline:** Single-field edits, toggles (use PatternFly Switch Checked with Label), renames

### Delete (Destructive) — Three Variants

ALWAYS use `ConfirmationDialog` from `src/components/ConfirmationDialog.tsx`. Never use raw `Modal` + `ModalHeader` + `ModalBody` + `ModalFooter` for delete actions.

All delete variants share: Small modal, warning icon title, `confirmVariant="danger"`, `confirmLabel="Delete"`, cancel `variant="link"`, checkbox via `destructiveAcknowledgement` (Delete button disabled until checked).

**Simple Delete** — no downstream effects (role, policy, group, user, identity provider)
- Body: `"The [resource] [name in bold] will be deleted. This cannot be undone."`
- Checkbox: `"I understand this [resource] will be permanently deleted."`

**Cascade Delete** — other records get permanently deleted too (workflow → executions, tool provider → tools)
- Body: `"The [resource] [name in bold] will be deleted. This cannot be undone."`
- Body 2: `"Resources that will be deleted"` as a header, then one row per resource type with its own Badge count — e.g., "Executions [12]", "Tools [3]"
- Checkbox: `"I understand this [resource] and the resources shown above will be permanently deleted."`

**Ripple Effect Delete** — other resources break/become invalid but are not deleted (credential → referencing workflows fail, project → orphaned resources, workflow → parent workflows become invalid)
- Body: `"The [resource] [name in bold] will be deleted. This cannot be undone."`
- Body 2: `"Resources that will be affected"` as a header, then one row per resource type with its own Badge count — e.g., "Workflows [2]", "Credentials [5]"
- Checkbox: `"I understand this [resource] and the resources shown above will be affected by this deletion."`

> A resource can combine variants (e.g., workflow delete = cascade for executions + ripple for parent workflows). Show both Body 2 sections in that case.

- Post-delete: stay on list (from table), navigate back (from detail), show toast alert

### Remove/Unassign/Cancel/Stop (Destructive, Reversible)
- Modal variant: Small with warning icon
- Title: `"[Remove/Unassign/Cancel/Stop] [resource type]?"`
- Body: resource name and consequence
- Action button: `variant="danger"`
- Cancel button: `variant="link"`
- Post-cancel/stop: stay on list (from table), stay on details (from detail), show toast alert

### Disable (Non-Destructive)
- Use standard confirmation modal (no warning icon, no danger button)
- Modal variant: Small (PatternFly Small Variant Modal)
- Title: `"Disable [resource type]?"`
- Body: `"You are about to disable the [resource type] [name in bold]. You can re-enable the [resource type] at any time."`
- Confirm button: `variant="primary"`
- Cancel button: `variant="link"`
- Post-disable: stay on list (from table), stay on details (from detail), show toast alert

## Feedback & Notifications

### Success Feedback
- Use PatternFly's Dismissible Success Toast Alert for success messages after create, update, delete actions
- Toast alerts should auto-dismiss after a reasonable duration
- Message format: `"[Resource type] [action] successfully"`

### Error Feedback
- Page-level loading errors: use `useQueryState(query, { title: '...', onRetry: ... })` — hooks up `ErrorState` with retry automatically
- Mutation errors: use `useMutationErrorHandler` — wires up `ErrorState` and toast alerts automatically
- Form validation errors: use inline field-level errors via PatternFly's Validated component

### Loading States
- Use PatternFly's Spinner component during async operations
- Page-level: centered spinner in content area
- Button actions: loading spinner on the button, disable during operation
- Tables: skeleton or spinner while data loads

## Button Placement Rules

Button alignment differs by context (follows PatternFly convention):

| Context | Primary action position |
|---|---|
| Page headers | **Rightmost** |
| Modals | **Leftmost** (Cancel link on right) |
| Forms (full page) | **Leftmost** (Cancel link on right) |
| Toolbars | **Leftmost** (kebab menu on far right) |

## Modals

- Use PatternFly's Small Variant Modal
- Delete modals use Title Icon Modal
- Buttons: left-aligned, primary → secondary → tertiary
- Cancel button is `variant="link"` when paired with primary action
- This applies to all modals, including delete confirmations

## Bulk Actions

- Use PatternFly Selectable with Checkbox Table
- Expandable table column order: expand/collapse chevron → checkbox → table columns
- Bulk actions in kebab menu in toolbar (right of primary button)
- Delete/remove option is always last
- Always include bulk action confirmation modal

## Statuses and Labels

- **Statuses:** PatternFly Outline Status Label component
- **Labels/Tags:** PatternFly Filled Non-status Label component, default to gray
- If labels on a table reference a resource, make them clickable, navigating to the details page

## Icons

All icons MUST come from the Red Hat Design System (RHDS) icon set, NOT standard PatternFly defaults. The project uses Compass and Unified Theme frameworks.

## Expand/Collapse Chevrons

- Use PatternFly Expandable Table component

## Content Rules

- **Sentence case** by default everywhere
- **Title case** only for navigation items and page titles
- **User-generated strings** are displayed exactly as entered — do not transform casing

## Workflow Builder

- Based on React Flow with PatternFly as visual wrapper
- Canvas built left to right
- Single click: select/expand/collapse step
- Double click: open panel view with Input/Output info
- Right click: same as kebab menu
- Add step: opens side panel, auto-adjusts canvas
- Run workflow: single trigger → plain Run button; multiple triggers → dropdown for trigger selection; confirmation dialog with "Don't show again", then `RunWorkflowModal` JSON editor for mock trigger data
- Test step (Run step): from node kebab menu → choice dialog → mock data editor (CodeEditor with JSON); upstream nodes mocked as "skipped"; results in execution visualizer
- Canvas controls: anchored to bottom-left corner
- Canvas node cards: fixed 240px width — use `overflow-wrap: anywhere` on all dynamic text (`Title`, `Content`) to prevent overflow
- View-only views: Run view, Run history, Version history

## Accessibility Guidelines

Achieving full WCAG 2.1 AA and Section 508 compliance requires careful implementation beyond PatternFly's built-in component accessibility. Developers are responsible for contextual accessibility:

### Semantic HTML & Page Structure
- Proper heading hierarchy (`<h1>`–`<h6>`) without skipping levels
- Use semantic tags (`<main>`, `<nav>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`, `<aside>`) or ARIA landmark roles

### Keyboard Navigation & Focus Management
- Every interactive element must be fully keyboard-operable
- Never remove focus outline without providing a visible alternative (3:1 contrast ratio)
- Manage focus programmatically on route changes and modal open/close
- Trap focus inside modals until dismissed; return focus to trigger on close

### Dynamic Content & State Changes
- Use `aria-live` (`polite` or `assertive`) for dynamic updates (job status, toasts)
- Use `aria-expanded`, `aria-disabled`, `aria-current` for state communication

### Forms & Error Handling
- Every input must have an associated `<label>` (not just placeholder text)
- Use `aria-invalid="true"` and `aria-describedby` to link inputs to error messages

### Color, Contrast, and Iconography
- Text and icons: 4.5:1 contrast for normal text, 3:1 for large text/UI components
- Never convey information by color alone — include icons and descriptive text
- Use `alt=""` or `aria-hidden="true"` for decorative images

### Testing
- Automated: accessibility tools in unit tests and CI/CD
- Manual: keyboard-only testing with Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Space, Arrow keys
- Screen reader: verify actual user experience with assistive technology

## Styling Rules

### No Global, Unscoped CSS

NEVER write global CSS rules that target element types, PatternFly class names, or broad selectors. Global styles bleed across component boundaries, silently override design tokens, and break theming and upgrade-compatibility.

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.pf-v6-c-menu__item { min-height: 0; }
p { margin-bottom: 8px; }

/* ✅ GOOD — scoped CSS Module */
/* MyComponent.module.css */
.menuItem { min-height: 0; }
```

### Styling Priority Order

1. **PatternFly props/variants** — use built-in props (`variant`, `isCompact`, `hasNoPadding`, etc.) first
2. **PF6 design tokens** — use `var(--pf-t--global--*)` for spacing, color, sizing; never hardcoded `px`
3. **CSS Modules** (`.module.css`) — scoped overrides only; never use `:global()` inside a module
4. **Inline `style` prop** — only for dynamic values computed at runtime

### Exceptions

If a global style seems necessary, follow the PatternFly gaps process: check PF docs/tokens → raise with UX → engage PatternFly upstream. Approved exceptions must be documented with a `patternfly-override` Jira label.
